@startuml
title Serviqo - Module 5: Job Tracking & Communication

left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor Customer
actor Worker
actor "Realtime Socket Service" as Realtime

rectangle "Serviqo Job Tracking & Communication" {
  usecase "Track a job's status" as TrackJob
  usecase "View job history and\ncurrent status" as ViewHistory
  usecase "Track open, active/\nassigned and completed stages" as StatusStages
  usecase "Confirm job completion" as ConfirmCompletion

  usecase "Communicate about a job" as Communicate
  usecase "View conversations\nand message history" as ViewMessages
  usecase "Send and receive messages" as ExchangeMessages
  usecase "Mark received messages\nas read" as MarkRead

  usecase "Receive real-time job,\nbid and message updates" as ReceiveUpdates
}

Customer -- TrackJob
Worker -- TrackJob
Customer -- ConfirmCompletion
Customer -- Communicate
Worker -- Communicate

TrackJob ..> ViewHistory : <<include>>
TrackJob ..> StatusStages : <<include>>
ConfirmCompletion ..> TrackJob : <<extend>>

Communicate ..> ViewMessages : <<include>>
Communicate ..> ExchangeMessages : <<include>>
ViewMessages ..> MarkRead : <<include>>
ExchangeMessages -- Realtime

ReceiveUpdates -- Customer
ReceiveUpdates -- Worker
ReceiveUpdates -- Realtime

note right of ConfirmCompletion
Only the customer who owns an active
job can confirm it as completed.
The completion update is delivered
to the customer and assigned worker.
end note

note bottom of StatusStages
An accepted bid assigns a worker and
moves the job to active. The customer
can then mark it completed. Open is
the posted, bid-accepting stage.
end note

note bottom of ReceiveUpdates
Job status, bid decisions, and new
messages are distributed in real time
through authenticated Socket.IO user rooms.
end note

@enduml
